WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Good morning John and welcome to this special report from the Vlogbrothers newsroom.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:10.180
Today, January 3rd, 2014 at 10:00 AM Pacific Time, the Golden Gate Bridge did not collapse.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:17.480
110,000 vehicles were safely conveyed over 8,000 feet from one side of the bridge to the other,

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:24.760
including cars, trucks, semi-trucks, not even to mention the countless bicyclists and pedestrians.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.920
The bridge did not collapse, despite being exposed to harsh weather conditions and constant vibrations

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.640
for more than 76 years.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.560
The death count at this point is unknown, but is thought to be zero.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.320
Thanks for sharing all the good news John, and there is so much good news. But there's also bad news.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.180
Including the fact that many people seem to be physically incapable of believing that there is good news

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.720
in the world. There were a lot of comments on your video and I'm not saying all, but a lot saying things like:

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.880
"Divorce rates are only down because the economy is in shambles and people can't afford them anymore."

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:53.380
NOPE.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.280
"Infant mortality's only down because there are more abortions being performed."

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.600
"Yeah, people are getting cured of more diseases but there are more diseased people."

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.500
"Well, my Internet speeds didn't get any faster, so I don't believe it."

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.920
It does actually seem hard to believe that the world is getting better and there are reasons for that.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.000
And it's not just cable news, which we love to complain about.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.120
#1: Psychology.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.480
Studies show that we weigh bad stuff happening to us about two times more heavily than we weigh good stuff,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.600
which means that we have to have, like, two times more good stuff happen to us just to think that the world

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.740
is good and we have bad stuff happen to us.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.360
Second: Probability.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.200
So if your newspaper only covered you and the 1,000 nearest people to you, there would be about

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:36.140
one murder per lifetime, but as we expand that circle to all seven billion people on the Earth,

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:42.440
there are terrible things happening pretty much every moment of every day. Terrible and unusual,

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:48.260
which our brains like to know about just in case they might affect us, and so we pay attention to all of it,

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.180
and it's just too much.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.960
#3: Entropy.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:57.840
Things fall apart, destroying stuff is easy, building it is hard. The universe tends to disorder, so just keeping

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:04.000
stuff from falling down is hard. like, everyday, the Golden Gate Bridge doesn't collapse is a victory that goes

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.540
uncelebrated. And yet, mostly bad stuff doesn't happen, so we are constantly surrounded by good news,

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.880
which makes it pretty boring, so we don't talk about it. Part of the big psychological theory of mind is that our

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.880
brains pick out unusual things and focus on them and so we don't think about all of the great stuff

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.420
that just works and happens and no problems. There's gas in the gas station and food at the grocery store.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.840
#4: Good is gradual.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:32.560
Bad stuff happens in spikes. Like, stock markets crash. They don't crash upwards, just down.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.640
There's no good equivalent of a terrorist attack. You can't crash a cancer cure into a hospital and just

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.400
*Pwsh* everybody's better, can't go to the airport with a gun that shoots healthy kidneys and then shoot a bunch

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.840
late stage diabetics. Kidneys just flying inside of people. Plt Plt Plt. Plt. I got four now!

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.240
Good stuff happens gradually over a long period of time. And that's okay.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.760
Finally, #5: Bias.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.520
All these factors pile up on each other and we start to believe that only bad stuff ever happens in the world

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.160
and once we believe that, we only take into account information that reinforces it.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.600
This is cognitive bias called confirmation bias, which I think is why a lot of people were trying to poke holes

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.360
in what you said in your last video John, because it didn't fit with the worldview of "The world is messed up and

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.400
broken and going downhill like crazy." And so you try and figure out why that isn't the case

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:25.080
when in fact, it just is. The world's okay. I'm not saying though that it's all unicorns and Sherlock premieres.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.580
Income inequality in the US is ridiculous. We have the highest incarceration rate in the world,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:35.220
and global climate change is going to threaten the stability of everything. I've got nothing against caution,

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:40.060
we should be cautious. But we should also not be pessimistic, because that's just going to hold us back.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.740
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.960
I drew these things on the back of Hanklerfish drawings, so if you got a Hanklerfish drawing,

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.620
there's a chance that you will get one of these. And if you're interested in psychology, which is a lot of what

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.120
we were talking about in this video, I am pleased to announce that the next season of Crash Course,

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:59.030
I will be doing Crash Course psychology. Also, go subscribe to Grace's new channel, youtube.com/itsgrace

